# RULE: Version And Release Sync

Single source of truth: `package.json` → `version` (Electron `app.getVersion()`, installer names, update check).

## When agents MUST bump version

After a **completed user-visible feature** or **release cut** (WU gate / handoff closed), not per intermediate commit.

| Change | SemVer (pre-1.0) | Example |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Bug fix, no new UX | PATCH | `0.0.1` → `0.0.2` |
| New user-visible feature (Registry `implemented`) | MINOR | `0.0.2` → `0.1.0` |
| Breaking host API, settings schema v2, removed flow | MAJOR | `0.x` → `1.0.0` |

Do **not** bump for: refactors, tests-only, docs-only, reviewer-only, planned→in-progress Registry edits.

## Files to update together

On version bump:

1. `package.json` — `version` field only (name stays `OmniCall`)
2. `CHANGELOG.md` — release section for `X.Y.Z`
3. `npm run release:sync-manifest` — dev copies + `distribution/update-manifest.json` (published to **omnicall-releases**)
4. Work-history entry — note new version if shipping

Rebuild installers (`npm run build:*`) only when cutting a **distribution** release, not for every dev commit.

## Release checklist (human or `/release` agent)

1. `npm run release:preflight`
2. Bump `package.json` per SemVer table
3. `npm run release:sync-manifest`
4. Commit on `main` → `git tag v<version>` → push `main` + tag
5. CI `release.yml` publishes installers to **HailRase/omnicall-releases** (secret `OMNICALL_RELEASES_TOKEN`)

Playbook: `guides/RELEASE-PLAYBOOK.md`. Migration: `guides/Distribution-Migration-Checklist.md`. Contract: `guides/Manual-Update-Manifest.md`.
